cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Compounding heritable genetic disorders of military toxicant
  exposure: an interactive evidence map
message: >-
  If you use this work, or cite the connections it maps, please
  cite it as below.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Daniel
    family-names: Trujillo
    name-particle: Joaquin
    affiliation: GANTASMO
    city: Las Vegas
    region: Nevada
    country: US
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/danieljtrujillo/military-chemical-exposure-and-multigenerational-genotoxic-compounding
url: >-
  https://danieljtrujillo.github.io/military-chemical-exposure-and-multigenerational-genotoxic-compounding/
abstract: >-
  An interactive, cited map of the relationships between military
  and industrial toxicant exposure and heritable disease across
  generations. Six exposures (dioxin/TCDD, hexavalent chromium,
  ammonium perchlorate, naturally occurring asbestos, ionizing
  radiation, and hydrazine/UDMH) are linked to fifteen conditions
  through shared molecular pathways, with every exposure-to-disease
  link graded for evidence strength against published literature.
  Includes mechanisms of mutagenesis, transgenerational epigenetic
  inheritance, treatment options, and United States legal and
  financial resources for affected families.
keywords:
